---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Showcase — HarvTech"
  description="Working portfolio pieces — this site, the secure-AI-landing-zone lab, and more."
>
  <section class="container-page py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Showcase</p>
    <h1 class="title-display mb-6 hero-gradient max-w-3xl leading-tight">
      Working portfolio.
    </h1>
    <p class="body-muted mb-12 max-w-2xl text-lg">
      Public projects, with the source on GitHub and the trade-offs
      written up in plain English. Detailed case studies dropping in
      one by one.
    </p>

    <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card p-7">
        <span class="badge-accent mb-3 inline-block">Live</span>
        <p class="title-card mt-3 mb-2">harvtech.co.uk infrastructure</p>
        <p class="body-muted mb-4 text-sm">
          This site. Astro + Tailwind output, served from Azure Storage
          $web, behind Front Door with WAF. Terraform across two stacks
          with OIDC-federated CI/CD. The git history is intentionally
          honest about what worked first time and what didn't.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/HarvtechUK/harvtech-site"
          rel="noopener"
          target="_blank"
          class="btn-secondary text-sm"
        >
          View the repo
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-7">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3">In progress</p>
        <p class="title-card mb-2">Secure AI Landing Zone</p>
        <p class="body-muted text-sm">
          Reference Terraform for an Azure OpenAI / Foundry workload
          with private endpoints, Entra Conditional Access, Defender
          for Cloud, AKS image scanning, and WAF in front of the app
          tier. Coming as a separate repo with this site as its case
          study home.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
